most low fat diets are based on the idea  that saturated fat should be avoided  this is because in the 60s and 70s  researchers found out that saturated fat  raises cholesterol and cholesterol had  already been linked to heart disease but  saturated fat actually raises good types  of cholesterol and recent studies have  suggested it doesn't seriously effect  the bad types consumed in moderation  it's more of a neutral energy source  with no direct link to heart problems  nutritionists have often grouped  saturated and trans fats together  calling them bad fats but while these  fats might resemble each other in  appearance their effects on you are  completely different saturated fats  aren't inherently damaging but trans  fats can lower your good cholesterol  raise your bad cholesterol and cause  insulin resistance and heart problems  it's this partially hydrogenated variety  that you need to watch out for some  foods are described as healthy because  of their high levels of unsaturated fats  unlike the saturated and trans varieties  most unsaturated fats don't raise your  bad cholesterol or risk of heart disease  the right ones can even help lower them  but there are different types of  unsaturated fats and while some are  heart-healthy others can be really bad  for you if consumed in excess a typical  batch of canola oil contains a huge  amount of these questionable fats at  high doses it definitely shouldn't be  considered a health food  as it turns out low-fat diets might  actually be worse for you when people  cut out fats they tend to replace it  with sugar and refined carbs these  things have been proven to lower your  good cholesterol and make the bad  varieties even worse there is in fact no  evidence that low fat diets have any  actual benefits they were based on an  assumption that science has proven wrong  it's easy to see why people would think  eating fat makes you fat but the truth  is a little more complicated fat may be  high in calories but it actually fills  you up much faster than protein and  carbs this is why high fat low carb  diets are often more effective than low  fat diets though food advertising  continues to take advantage of common  myths about fats moderate amounts of  natural varieties can definitely fit  into a healthy lifestyle
 

